    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup optimized to exploit the vulnerabilities of the Burrows rotation, as evidenced by our top-rated play, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). He carries our highest daily efficiency score, buoyed by a significant +17% SP Skill boost and a favorable platoon matchup. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (72.41) provides elite utility value; he benefits from an 86% SB-favorable delivery cadence from Brandon Pfaadt, making him a critical engine for our scarcity-driven focus on stolen bases. While **Kyle Tucker** (67.05) remains a pillar of our outfield, his efficiency is marginally tempered by his spot in the batting order, though his pedigree keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier against Kyle Freeland.\n\nStrategic depth remains a concern as we navigate injury headwinds, with **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco** all sidelined on the IL. Consequently, our bench is largely comprised of long-term holds like **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Sam Antonacci**, none of whom offered a viable path into today\u2019s starting nine. The most difficult decision rested on **Nasim Nunez** (58.62), who sits on the lower end of our starting threshold. While his speed and switch-hitting profile align with our roster philosophy, his #9 spot in the lineup constrained his score, placing him just ahead of **Dominic Smith** (53.44) in our internal rankings. We are monitoring the 34% rain risk in the **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith** matchup; if that game is flagged for delay, we may need to pivot to the depth provided by **Miguel Vargas** or **Coby Mayo** to protect our daily game caps. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.90) and **Heliot Ramos** (51.44) round out a balanced attack, with **Heliot Ramos** specifically highlighted for his potential to exploit the slow delivery of Kevin Gausman in pursuit of steals.",
